id: bootloader_smp_switch
label: Bootloader SMP Switch
package: bootloader
description: >
  Enables SMP (Switch Multi-Protocol) two-page switch record for dual-application
  bootloader configurations. The bootloader reads a switch record from two dedicated
  flash pages and boots the selected application (App 1 or App 2). This allows two
  independent applications to share the same device with the bootloader managing which
  one runs at boot. Applications can use the Flash API to request switching to the other
  application on next boot. If secure boot verification fails for the selected app, the
  bootloader automatically attempts to boot the alternate app as a fallback.
  Configure page base addresses, application base addresses, and default app in
  btl_smp_cfg.h.
category: Platform|Bootloader|Core
quality: production
metadata:
  sbom:
    license: MSLA
provides:
- name: bootloader_smp_switch
requires:
- name: bootloader_core
- name: bootloader_crc
root_path: bootloader/platform/bootloader
config_file:
- path: config/btl_smp_cfg.h
source:
- path: core/smp_switch/btl_smp_switch_record.c
define:
- name: BTL_SMP_SUPPORT
  value: 1
include:
- path: core/smp_switch
  file_list:
  - path: btl_smp_switch_record.h


